## Reliability caveats
- `p_local_bucket` is BUCKET-LEVEL empirical precision (1 - local FDR), NOT a per-pair probability (Codex #3). It ignores anchor count, coverage, length asymmetry, shelf/dup signals.
- The chunk-shuffle null assumes decoy-real chance rate == unrelated real-real chance rate; the CHUNK=12/25 envelope is the conservative mitigation of the unsettled chunk size (Codex #4).
- Verification runs on UNMASKED streams, so canonical text can re-enter a window near an anchor; `mask_ov_a/mask_ov_b` let consumers drop rows whose evidence is mostly masked (Codex #5).
- Decoys inflate DF by the injected fraction (~2%), mildly tightening the DF<=100 cap vs a pure production run.
- `dup_shelf`/`dup_lines` flag same-object joins (Codex R4): these are FINDS for a scholar, kept and flagged, not dropped.

